Task 3 — select only the wheel-compatible Python

Why:
- the runtime must execute the exact CPython implementation and minor recorded by the wheelhouse;
- Finder-launched macOS applications do not inherit the terminal PATH, while Windows executable lookup requires a controlled `.exe` suffix.

Implementation:
- strict bounded RuntimeManifest and closed RuntimeError categories;
- one Python PATH authority reuses agent_local::shell_environment, applies it to lookup, probes, venv creation and venv commands, and never mutates the process PATH;
- exact probes accept only CPython with the manifest major/minor and time out after five seconds;
- Unix lookup requires executable files; Windows lookup appends only the program-controlled `.exe` suffix and keeps `py -3.14` as separate arguments;
- Wheelhouse is exposed only after regular-file, manifest, stamp and allowed-entry validation;
- runtime installation is offline-only with `--no-index --find-links`.

